{"url": "https://bioe.umd.edu/graduate/prospective-students/financial-support", "final_url": "https://bioe.umd.edu/graduate/prospective-students/financial-support", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-23", "text": "Financial Support | Fischell Department of Bioengineering\nSkip to main content\nThe Fischell Department of Bioengineering at the A. James Clark School of Engineering, University of Maryland\nMobile Navigation Trigger\nSearch this site for:\nHome\nMain Menu\nMobile Navigation Trigger Reverse\neng.umd.edu\nContact\nApply\nGive\nCreative Ways to Give\nRecruit\nAbout\nMission\nFaculty and Staff\nAdvisory Board\nStrategic Plan\nThe Fischells\nCommunity Engagement & Development Committee\nUndergraduate\nB.S. in Bioengineering\nTracks\nCourses\nSample Plan\nTechnical Electives\nB.S. in Biocomputational Engineering\nB.S/M.S. Program\nProspective Students\nFirst Year Applicants\nTransfer Applicants\nAdmissions & Financial Aid\nStudent Groups\nCurrent Students\nAdvising & Support\nAdvising Forms\nApplying for Graduation\nAcademic Difficulty\nAdvising References\nTutoring & Study Resources\nStudent Groups\nScholarships & Awards\nHonors Program\nApplication Process\nFAQ\nCapstone\nAccreditation\nGraduate\nDegrees\nDoctor of Philosophy\nMaster of Science\nMaster of Engineering\nDoctor of Medicine/Doctor of Philosophy\nDoctor of Medicine/Master of Science\nProspective Students\nAdmissions\nFinancial Support\nInternational Applicants\nCurrent Students\nAdvising & Support\nInternational Students\nScholarships & Fellowships\nCourses\nFuture Faculty Program\nResearch\nInstitutes, Centers & Labs\nResearch Areas\nResearch News\nResearch Opportunities\nResearch Support\nAlumni & Industry\nAlumni Network\nPartner with BIOE\nNews\nPress Releases\nPublications Archive\nThe Catalyst\nEvents\nSeminars\nFall 2018 Seminars\nThe Bioengineering Seminar Series\nThe Bioengineering Seminar Series\neng.umd.edu\nContact\nApply\nGive\nCreative Ways to Give\nRecruit\nCED Committee\nCurrent and Ongoing Initiatives\nFaculty Directory\nStaff Directory\nCareers\nMedia\nFacilities\nClarkNet\nDepartment Forms\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYoutube\nLinkedin\nHome\nGraduate\nProspective Students\nFinancial Support\nFinancial Support\nThe department is committed to supporting PhD students for the duration of their studies. For the first year, top entering students are offered a fellowship financial package comprised of an annual stipend (approximately $40K), tuition remission (10 credits each semester), and access to subsidized employee health benefits. Subsequent years' support is renewed with satisfactory academic and research progress, and is typically provided from faculty advisor research funds in the form of a Graduate Research Assistantship with the same fringe benefits described above.\nA variety of fellowship opportunities are available, with a few examples listed below.\nNSF Graduate Research Fellowship\nPh.D. applicants are strongly encouraged to submit applications for the NSF Graduate Research Fellowship program in parallel with application for UMD admission and support.\nOther Fellowship Opportunities\nThe University of Maryland Graduate School and the A. James Clark School of Engineering offer additional fellowship enhancement packages for recruiting outstanding students. Typically, departments must nominate candidates to the College or Graduate School, and additional review and selection is required. Examples of these packages, which many of our students have won, include:\nDean's Fellowships\nWarren Citrin Fellowship\nFlagship Fellowship\nRonald E. McNair Graduate Fellowship\nTop\nCED Committee\nCurrent and Ongoing Initiatives\nFaculty Directory\nStaff Directory\nCareers\nMedia\nFacilities\nClarkNet\nDepartment Forms\nFacebook\nTwitter\nInstagram\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\numd.edu\n\u00a9 2026 University of Maryland", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://bioe.umd.edu/graduate/prospective-students/financial-support#main-conte